WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.376 --> 00:00:01.427
- Forget about the money.

00:00:01.427 --> 00:00:03.835
When you see the smile on a person's face,

00:00:03.835 --> 00:00:06.098
it's the greatest job in the world.

00:00:06.098 --> 00:00:07.661
I'm the first one in the office every day.

00:00:07.661 --> 00:00:10.495
I'm the last one in the office every day.

00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:12.491
It's a passion of mine, real estate.

00:00:12.491 --> 00:00:14.312
It's not just opening up a door

00:00:14.312 --> 00:00:17.570
and letting somebody walk
around and look at a house.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.812
That's not what I do.

00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:20.918
Some realtors do that,

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:22.660
I just feel like that's wrong.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.539
- He's an American real estate agent,

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.945
real estate investor, and
reality TV personality.

00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:30.665
He appears on the television
show Million Dollar Listing

00:00:30.665 --> 00:00:31.919
on the Bravo network.

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:34.894
In 2013, he was ranked as the number 30

00:00:34.894 --> 00:00:38.035
real estate agent in the country
by the Wall Street Journal

00:00:38.035 --> 00:00:41.286
with sales of over $200 million.

00:00:41.286 --> 00:00:42.958
He's Josh Altman, and here's my take

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:45.105
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:45.105 --> 00:00:46.727
Rule number one is my personal favorite.

00:00:46.727 --> 00:00:48.820
And as always, if Josh
something that really, really

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.386
resonates with you, please
leave it in the comments below

00:00:51.386 --> 00:00:52.909
and put quotes around it so other people

00:00:52.909 --> 00:00:55.781
can be inspired as well, enjoy.

00:00:55.781 --> 00:00:58.550
(whooshing)

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.133
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.811 --> 00:01:11.428
- Number one, you all can tell,

00:01:11.428 --> 00:01:12.780
you got to love what you do,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.880
and I love what I do, I love real estate.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.558
My favorite part about what
I do that I'm so excited

00:01:19.558 --> 00:01:21.817
every morning to wake up to is that time

00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:24.198
when you get to pass the keys over

00:01:24.198 --> 00:01:26.911
to a new buyer of a home,
and they actually bought

00:01:26.911 --> 00:01:30.324
the home, and you see the
smile on those people's faces,

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:32.527
okay, that's priceless.

00:01:32.527 --> 00:01:33.867
You can forget about all the other stuff,

00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:34.915
forget about the money.

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:37.401
When you see the smile on a person's face,

00:01:37.401 --> 00:01:39.619
it's the greatest job in the world.

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:42.738
Think about it, we help people achieve

00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:45.501
the American dream,
which is owning a home.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:46.855
And we get to be part of that.

00:01:46.855 --> 00:01:49.145
And if you're part of that, those people

00:01:49.145 --> 00:01:51.206
love you forever.

00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:52.469
- You know, you give
this great example of how

00:01:52.469 --> 00:01:54.864
you were on the treadmill
next to Tyler Perry,

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:56.943
and you were bold, you
kind of talked him up,

00:01:56.943 --> 00:01:59.849
you ended up selling his house.

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:01.529
But you approached him, and
you said, "Are you ready

00:02:01.529 --> 00:02:02.962
"to sell one of your houses?"

00:02:02.962 --> 00:02:04.767
You already knew that he owned two houses,

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:07.059
you knew were they were,
you know, so isn't that

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:09.350
also a big part of
this, you have to really

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.183
do the hard work?

00:02:10.183 --> 00:02:13.309
- Yeah, and really preparing
yourself to be lucky,

00:02:13.309 --> 00:02:16.816
putting yourself in situations
where you can get lucky,

00:02:16.816 --> 00:02:19.256
where it's not so much
luck, it's preparation.

00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:21.416
I tell a story about
how I'm standing inside

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:24.413
a line in Starbucks, and
I'm not at that Starbucks

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:26.167
'cause I like coffee,
I'm at that Starbucks

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:28.423
'cause that's where all
the wealthy people and all

00:02:28.423 --> 00:02:31.116
the celebrities in Beverly
Hills go every morning.

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.043
I meet a guy in line in
front of me, I end up

00:02:33.043 --> 00:02:34.793
showing him a house later that afternoon,

00:02:34.793 --> 00:02:36.516
and he buys a $12 million house.

00:02:36.516 --> 00:02:38.053
Some people would say that's luck.

00:02:38.053 --> 00:02:40.450
For me, it's all about
being in the right place,

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.320
and there was a reason why I'm there,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.900
because I'm an expert in my community

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.118
and I put myself in that situation.

00:02:46.118 --> 00:02:48.878
I always say in order to be
a successful salesperson,

00:02:48.878 --> 00:02:50.637
you got to know your product.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.182
Okay, that's the
single-most important thing,

00:02:52.182 --> 00:02:54.383
you got to know it like
the back of your hand.

00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:56.075
Otherwise you can't truly sell it,

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.084
and you got to believe in it as well.

00:02:57.084 --> 00:02:58.533
- 'Cause you don't believe
in it if you don't know it.

00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:02.125
- Right, exactly, so I am very, very good,

00:03:02.125 --> 00:03:04.560
and I can look anybody in
this business in the world

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.882
in the eyes and say I am
an expert at Los Angeles

00:03:07.882 --> 00:03:12.049
real estate, I study it,
I know more than 99.9999%

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.522
of the people out there, okay?

00:03:14.522 --> 00:03:16.718
I've flipped houses, I've financed houses,

00:03:16.718 --> 00:03:19.159
I sell houses, buy 'em, all that stuff.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:21.887
So I'm very confident
because I'm very good

00:03:21.887 --> 00:03:23.560
at what I do because I'm an expert,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:24.393
and I work very hard at it.

00:03:24.393 --> 00:03:25.665
- You do the work to become the expert.

00:03:25.665 --> 00:03:27.099
- It's not just falling on the lap.

00:03:27.099 --> 00:03:29.272
It's I'm the first one
in the office every day,

00:03:29.272 --> 00:03:32.157
I'm the last one in the office every day.

00:03:32.157 --> 00:03:33.930
It's a passion of mine, real estate,

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:37.088
so I don't consider it work,
but I literally study it.

00:03:37.088 --> 00:03:38.909
They call me the Rain Man of real estate.

00:03:38.909 --> 00:03:40.522
- There you go, I like it.

00:03:40.522 --> 00:03:43.163
- It's like how much is
a house on the 900 block

00:03:43.163 --> 00:03:45.043
in the flats of Beverly Hills?

00:03:45.043 --> 00:03:45.927
- And you can be within like

00:03:45.927 --> 00:03:46.760
a hundred thousand dollar range.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.137
- I could easily all day long.

00:03:48.137 --> 00:03:50.170
I feel it's super important these days

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.503
to be 24/7, okay?

00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:56.911
Alex had said it before, buying a house

00:03:56.911 --> 00:03:59.228
is the biggest investment
of somebody's life,

00:03:59.228 --> 00:04:01.038
99% of the time.

00:04:01.038 --> 00:04:02.525
Okay, that's a big deal.

00:04:02.525 --> 00:04:03.764
We do it every day.

00:04:03.764 --> 00:04:07.006
We forget how, you
know, nerveracking it is

00:04:07.006 --> 00:04:09.068
and how important it is to these people.

00:04:09.068 --> 00:04:11.631
So you have to make yourself available.

00:04:11.631 --> 00:04:13.697
You have to be 24/7.

00:04:13.697 --> 00:04:15.771
If I'm making a big investment,

00:04:15.771 --> 00:04:17.611
that person better be available to me.

00:04:17.611 --> 00:04:21.380
And there's a funny joke
because in Beverly Hills,

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.290
in a high-end market, you typically know

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.047
who you're going against
in a listing appointment.

00:04:26.047 --> 00:04:29.304
In fact, I think the last
10 listing appointments,

00:04:29.304 --> 00:04:31.615
the person has seen the other five agents,

00:04:31.615 --> 00:04:34.367
the same exact five agents every time.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.341
And you know, every once
in a while you get that

00:04:36.341 --> 00:04:38.028
awkward moment where you're walking out of

00:04:38.028 --> 00:04:41.975
a listing meeting, and the
new agent is walking in.

00:04:41.975 --> 00:04:44.225
And you give 'em this look.

00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:48.269
So it's very important to
be available, and what I do,

00:04:48.269 --> 00:04:50.477
a secret with that, when
all these people are meeting

00:04:50.477 --> 00:04:52.823
with these clients, and this
will be our little secret

00:04:52.823 --> 00:04:55.823
at ERA, you tell the client, listen,

00:04:56.947 --> 00:04:59.151
I want you to call me
and the other people,

00:04:59.151 --> 00:05:01.864
and I want you to see
who's available, okay?

00:05:01.864 --> 00:05:04.133
At random times throughout the day,

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.459
because I know that
these other high-end guys

00:05:06.459 --> 00:05:09.863
or girls, they're so, you
know, above everything,

00:05:09.863 --> 00:05:11.713
that they have secretaries and assistants

00:05:11.713 --> 00:05:13.755
and buyer's agents and this and that,

00:05:13.755 --> 00:05:16.601
and they don't give
their direct number out.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.240
And I pride myself in being available.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.586
Everybody has my cell phone,
I always pick up the call,

00:05:22.586 --> 00:05:24.012
and I think that's important to people.

00:05:24.012 --> 00:05:25.929
So that's a little trick that I use.

00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:28.858
I've always been, and to this day,

00:05:28.858 --> 00:05:30.498
the first person in the office

00:05:30.498 --> 00:05:32.314
and the last person to leave.

00:05:32.314 --> 00:05:34.326
I started out like everybody else,

00:05:34.326 --> 00:05:37.822
I walked up and down the
Hollywood Hills of Los Angeles

00:05:37.822 --> 00:05:41.090
till there were literally
no soles left on my shoes.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.932
I mean, that's how much I door-knocked.

00:05:42.932 --> 00:05:46.098
And I door-knocked every door,
and I really kept it basic,

00:05:46.098 --> 00:05:49.776
I cold-called nonstop for hours a day,

00:05:49.776 --> 00:05:52.474
and I lived by a schedule,
and I did that every day

00:05:52.474 --> 00:05:55.856
till slowly I'd pick up
one listing, then another,

00:05:55.856 --> 00:05:58.410
and then another, and you know,

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:02.185
next thing you know, it
starts to get more fun

00:06:02.185 --> 00:06:04.101
when you start making money, of course.

00:06:04.101 --> 00:06:06.811
But I started the same
way as everybody else,

00:06:06.811 --> 00:06:09.386
and I have people
underneath me that I mentor

00:06:09.386 --> 00:06:13.253
that I tell the same thing
to, you just got to start

00:06:13.253 --> 00:06:15.758
just to basics, you can't
watch Million Dollar Listing

00:06:15.758 --> 00:06:17.478
and think that all the
sudden you're going to make

00:06:17.478 --> 00:06:19.393
millions of dollars in real estate.

00:06:19.393 --> 00:06:22.520
you know, I've been in
some aspect of real estate

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:25.725
for over a decade now, so
this didn't happen over night.

00:06:25.725 --> 00:06:28.847
This is something that has been, you know,

00:06:28.847 --> 00:06:32.948
worked at nonstop, I've
studied the art of negotiation,

00:06:32.948 --> 00:06:37.451
I've studied how to read
people, I've really mastered

00:06:37.451 --> 00:06:40.026
my craft, and I take it very seriously.

00:06:40.026 --> 00:06:42.308
It's not just opening up a
door and letting somebody

00:06:42.308 --> 00:06:44.799
walk around and look at a house.

00:06:44.799 --> 00:06:46.197
That's not what I do.

00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:49.703
Some realtors do that, I
just feel like that's wrong.

00:06:49.703 --> 00:06:51.316
You got to sell the house.

00:06:51.316 --> 00:06:55.541
You got to, what I like to
say, sell the dream, right?

00:06:55.541 --> 00:06:57.137
You got to sell the dream.

00:06:57.137 --> 00:06:59.451
Most important is what I like to call

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:02.137
surround yourself with your dream team.

00:07:02.137 --> 00:07:04.490
I call it Josh Altman's Dream Team,

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:08.389
and it consists of a
good amount of support

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:11.217
from people that I trust,
value their opinion,

00:07:11.217 --> 00:07:12.733
and who I surround myself with.

00:07:12.733 --> 00:07:15.575
I always say that you are
the average of five people

00:07:15.575 --> 00:07:17.316
that you surround yourselves with, right?

00:07:17.316 --> 00:07:18.149
Did you ever hear that before?

00:07:18.149 --> 00:07:19.276
- Yeah.
- Yeah, I totally do.

00:07:19.276 --> 00:07:22.357
- (mumbles) to that?
- I totally did make that up.

00:07:22.357 --> 00:07:24.267
I just made that up right now.

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:27.079
So I think it's super
important to do that,

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:31.049
so in real estate, for
example, I have the best

00:07:31.049 --> 00:07:34.017
mortgage broker who's
available 24/7 for me,

00:07:34.017 --> 00:07:36.216
and we've worked our way up
in the business together.

00:07:36.216 --> 00:07:40.198
I have, you know, everybody
from the best title guy

00:07:40.198 --> 00:07:42.637
and escrow guy and all
that, so I surround myself

00:07:42.637 --> 00:07:45.174
with this team of people who I can trust

00:07:45.174 --> 00:07:46.920
and they can guide me
in the right directions

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.975
of whatever I do.

00:07:48.975 --> 00:07:51.059
So that's one way,
obviously, in any business,

00:07:51.059 --> 00:07:54.179
it's just surround yourself with people

00:07:54.179 --> 00:07:55.183
who support you.

00:07:55.183 --> 00:07:56.956
- What would you say to
somebody who hasn't found

00:07:56.956 --> 00:07:59.215
their work drug yet, who
hasn't found that thing

00:07:59.215 --> 00:08:00.383
that really inspires them?

00:08:00.383 --> 00:08:02.106
- Right, so the ultimate goal is obviously

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:03.897
to find something that you love to do,

00:08:03.897 --> 00:08:05.563
because it's not considered work anymore

00:08:05.563 --> 00:08:07.515
and it's not about money
anymore 'cause it's all about

00:08:07.515 --> 00:08:11.776
happiness and waking up
excited to do what you do.

00:08:11.776 --> 00:08:14.219
All these jobs that led
up to that, I always try

00:08:14.219 --> 00:08:17.490
to find the thing that I
loved most about each job

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:21.341
and really concentrate on
that and be the best at that.

00:08:21.341 --> 00:08:23.232
You got to go through a
lot of stepping stones

00:08:23.232 --> 00:08:24.770
in order to find the place.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.049
I worked at a funeral home.

00:08:27.049 --> 00:08:30.610
I was an assistant in the mail
room for a very long time.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.539
I had about a dozen jobs
which are not so much fun

00:08:33.539 --> 00:08:35.221
in order to find the right job.

00:08:35.221 --> 00:08:37.405
And that's going to be everybody's
going to go through that,

00:08:37.405 --> 00:08:39.989
so give it time,
concentrate on what you love

00:08:39.989 --> 00:08:41.968
about your job, and be the best at that.

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:43.781
I don' care what you do
for a living, I don't care

00:08:43.781 --> 00:08:44.881
if you're the biggest
celebrity in the world.

00:08:44.881 --> 00:08:47.123
I treat you the same
as somebody, you know,

00:08:47.123 --> 00:08:49.492
a newlywed couple who's
buying their first condo

00:08:49.492 --> 00:08:50.575
for $500,000.

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:54.380
I talk about it in my book,
you know, I used to be

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.786
a field goal kicker, so I always say

00:08:55.786 --> 00:08:57.409
kick every football the same.

00:08:57.409 --> 00:08:59.735
You treat every deal the
same, you treat everybody

00:08:59.735 --> 00:09:01.248
with the same respect,
and I think that's why

00:09:01.248 --> 00:09:03.408
people come back to us,
because we don't care

00:09:03.408 --> 00:09:05.027
if you're famous or not.

00:09:05.027 --> 00:09:07.123
They know that we're the
expert at what we do,

00:09:07.123 --> 00:09:09.313
and that we're the best at what we do.

00:09:09.313 --> 00:09:11.303
The most important thing,
and I tell it over and over

00:09:11.303 --> 00:09:15.049
and over and over again,
get a mentor, okay?

00:09:15.049 --> 00:09:17.032
When I first got into the business,

00:09:17.032 --> 00:09:20.876
the first few deals that
I ended up picking up

00:09:20.876 --> 00:09:25.124
were sitting open houses
of more successful agents

00:09:25.124 --> 00:09:27.111
that didn't have time to be everywhere.

00:09:27.111 --> 00:09:29.658
I said, listen, I'll do anything

00:09:29.658 --> 00:09:31.855
to help you out on your
properties, and you know,

00:09:31.855 --> 00:09:33.861
they'd say, okay, why
don't you sit at this house

00:09:33.861 --> 00:09:35.139
that weekend.

00:09:35.139 --> 00:09:37.822
And I'd end up picking
up buyers through them.

00:09:37.822 --> 00:09:42.238
It's very important to
have somebody guide you

00:09:42.238 --> 00:09:43.665
to be successful.

00:09:43.665 --> 00:09:46.843
Again, it's having someone next to you

00:09:46.843 --> 00:09:50.181
who's done it, has the
advice that you need,

00:09:50.181 --> 00:09:52.585
can kind of tell you the pros and the cons

00:09:52.585 --> 00:09:54.582
and what they should be concentrating on.

00:09:54.582 --> 00:09:57.230
Get a mentor, it's the
most important thing.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.607
All this coaching stuff that we do,

00:09:59.607 --> 00:10:02.278
there are reasons why we
do this, and it's very,

00:10:02.278 --> 00:10:06.974
very successful, it's been
successful for years and years.

00:10:06.974 --> 00:10:09.509
That would be the one
thing, if you can't make it,

00:10:09.509 --> 00:10:12.550
make sure you call somebody
who, or link up with someone

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.342
who can teach you the ropes.

00:10:14.342 --> 00:10:16.670
I thought that right now
would be the perfect time

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:20.718
to share a customer
service story with you.

00:10:20.718 --> 00:10:21.635
True story.

00:10:23.041 --> 00:10:27.614
Couple years ago, I got
a call from a young lady,

00:10:27.614 --> 00:10:29.569
and was all excited, she
tells me she's looking

00:10:29.569 --> 00:10:33.652
for a property, and then
she says the word lease.

00:10:35.391 --> 00:10:38.007
Our favorite words as realtors.

00:10:38.007 --> 00:10:40.007
I'm looking for a lease.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.653
Oh, you know, unless it's
an $85,000 a month lease,

00:10:44.653 --> 00:10:45.736
I don't know.

00:10:47.661 --> 00:10:50.000
But I was in a good mood,
so I took that call,

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.408
and I said, "Sure, I'll
help you find a lease."

00:10:53.408 --> 00:10:57.210
And turns out it was a
$5,000 a month lease.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.293
And I took her around for six months.

00:11:01.287 --> 00:11:03.610
(audience laughing)

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.693
The term was only a year.

00:11:07.754 --> 00:11:11.173
Anyways, I like to finish what I start.

00:11:11.173 --> 00:11:14.442
So I went through with it,
found her an amazing place,

00:11:14.442 --> 00:11:16.637
she couldn't be happier.

00:11:16.637 --> 00:11:18.770
In fact, she was so happy
that she called her father

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:22.091
that night, and she said,
"Dad, I got the greatest place.

00:11:22.091 --> 00:11:25.726
"My realtor's amazing, he
doesn't care about money at all."

00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:28.726
(audience laughing)

00:11:30.563 --> 00:11:34.031
And it happened to be that her father

00:11:34.031 --> 00:11:37.619
was sitting next to
the CEO of his company.

00:11:37.619 --> 00:11:41.320
And he heard the story, and that CEO said,

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:44.075
"Actually, I'm thinking
of selling my penthouse.

00:11:44.075 --> 00:11:46.850
"Maybe I should use that guy."

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.530
Sure enough, I went in, I met the CEO,

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.601
and I got the listing of his

00:11:49.601 --> 00:11:51.351
$4 million penthouse.

00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:55.378
(audience applauding)

00:11:56.795 --> 00:11:59.682
While I was sitting
that open house on that

00:11:59.682 --> 00:12:01.832
$4 million penthouse,
'cause that's my favorite

00:12:01.832 --> 00:12:04.749
thing to do, a celebrity walked in.

00:12:07.098 --> 00:12:09.252
And that celebrity walked
around, and he checked out

00:12:09.252 --> 00:12:13.419
that incredible penthouse, and
he looked at me and he said,

00:12:14.255 --> 00:12:18.578
"Yeah, this is cool, do
you have anything cooler?"

00:12:18.578 --> 00:12:19.828
I said, "Sure."

00:12:20.862 --> 00:12:23.437
So I went back to the
office and I put together

00:12:23.437 --> 00:12:27.604
the list of the coolest
penthouses you could find.

00:12:28.704 --> 00:12:31.560
And I showed that celebrity around,

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.021
and that celebrity ended up buying

00:12:34.021 --> 00:12:36.104
an $11 million penthouse,

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:40.450
which broke the record for Santa Monica.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:45.095
So from that lease, that
$5,000 a month lease,

00:12:45.095 --> 00:12:48.349
which led to that $4
million penthouse sale,

00:12:48.349 --> 00:12:51.515
which led to that $11
million penthouse sale,

00:12:51.515 --> 00:12:54.543
and it is the gift that keeps on giving

00:12:54.543 --> 00:12:55.960
on and on and on.

00:12:57.667 --> 00:12:58.584
That is why

00:12:59.754 --> 00:13:01.575
customer service

00:13:01.575 --> 00:13:05.184
is so important to everybody's business.

00:13:05.184 --> 00:13:06.742
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:06.742 --> 00:13:10.017
I made this video because
Trevin or Trevon Clack

00:13:10.017 --> 00:13:10.853
asked me to.

00:13:10.853 --> 00:13:12.226
So if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you

00:13:12.226 --> 00:13:14.214
want me to profile next, leave it down

00:13:14.214 --> 00:13:16.043
in the comments below, and
I'll see what I can do.

00:13:16.043 --> 00:13:18.318
I'd also love to know what did Josh say

00:13:18.318 --> 00:13:20.066
that really resonated with you the most,

00:13:20.066 --> 00:13:22.260
what rule was most impactful to you,

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.516
what are you going to apply
to your life or your business?

00:13:24.516 --> 00:13:26.356
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:13:26.356 --> 00:13:27.981
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:27.981 --> 00:13:30.227
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Krypton Kho,

00:13:30.227 --> 00:13:32.532
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:13:32.532 --> 00:13:34.952
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:13:34.952 --> 00:13:36.598
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:13:36.598 --> 00:13:38.554
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:13:38.554 --> 00:13:40.336
to believe in yourselves

00:13:40.336 --> 00:13:42.549
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:42.549 --> 00:13:44.905
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:13:44.905 --> 00:13:47.238
(whooshing)

